contributed to sensorimotor polyneuropathy, which is rare-
ly described despite being related to SPS (it was found in 
1/10 UK patients as reported by Kass-Iliyya et al., 2021).  
In our opinion, polyneuropathy, its axonal component in 
particular, may reduce the severity of axial symptoms of  
the disease mainly in the distal parts of the lower limbs  
by causing damage to the reflex arc, both in the outward 
and inward parts.
No complications of anaesthesia were observed in our pa -
tient despite a relative high number of surgical interventions.
We hope that this case report will contribute to the knowl-
edge on SPS and broaden the awareness of practicing phy-
sicians.
